# Cursor Rules for Next.js GitHub Users Project

## Project Overview

This is a Next.js 15 project using TypeScript, React Query, SCSS Modules, and a feature-based architecture. Follow these patterns consistently.

## File Structure & Organization

### Feature-Based Architecture

- Organize code by features in the `features/` directory
- Each feature should have its own `ui/`, `lib/`, `contexts/`, `queries/`, `services/`, and `server/` subdirectories as needed
- Shared code goes in `features/shared/`
- Use `types/` directory for TypeScript type definitions organized by domain

### Example Folder Structure

```
project-root/
├── app/                          # Next.js App Router
│   ├── [id]/                    # Dynamic routes
│   │   └── page.tsx
│   ├── favs/
│   │   └── page.tsx
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   ├── page.tsx
│   └── providers.tsx
│
├── features/                     # Feature-based organization
│   ├── pages/                   # Page components
│   │   ├── SearchPage/
│   │   │   ├── SearchPage.tsx
│   │   │   └── SearchPage.module.scss
│   │   └── FavsPage/
│   │       ├── FavsPage.tsx
│   │       └── FavsPage.module.scss
│   │
│   ├── shared/                  # Shared across features
│   │   ├── constants/
│   │   │   └── index.tsx
│   │   ├── contexts/
│   │   │   └── SharedContext.tsx
│   │   ├── hooks/
